          Tip velocities >100 m/s drop local static pressure below liquid vapor pressure, nucleating vapor micro-voids that collapse with 1,000 m/s micro-jets.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Diagram 2: Steam Expansion in Closed Vessel -->
      <div class="p-5 bg-surface rounded-xl border border-hairline flex flex-col items-center">
        <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-2xl mb-3">
          💨
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink mb-1">Thermal Expansion &amp; Scald Risk</h4>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-body leading-relaxed">
          Trapped air expands by 25% while water boils into vapor expanding 1,600:1. In sealed bullet cups, this spikes internal pressure to over 15–20 PSI.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Diagram 3: Shaft Seal Lubricant Migration -->
      <div class="p-5 bg-surface rounded-xl border border-hairline flex flex-col items-center">
        <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-purple-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-2xl mb-3">
          ⚙️
        </div>
        <h4 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink mb-1">Shaft Lip Seal &amp; Bearing Wear</h4>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-body leading-relaxed">
          High-friction blade rotation degrades nitrile/silicone seals. As dynamic play exceeds 0.25 mm, industrial petroleum grease extrudes directly into purees.
        </p>
      </div>
